   "id": "DR-GAP-VISUAL",
   "element": "Visual storytelling events — plate mood + word fade (v4, doctrine pass 2026-10-24 ~17:35 ET)",
   "choice": "Line-scoped visual events so the picture performs the beat (visual-storytelling doctrine: word animation is a storytelling engine; sound-off the story must read from pictures + animated words). (1) L6 generations plate: brightness dips 16 % through the line's middle — the hunter dies — and recovers as his knowledge lives. (2) L8-L10 embers plate: dims 22 % across L8-L9 (forgetting wins), rekindles across L10 to +2 % at 'hard to kill'. (3) L9's words fade to ~45 % inside each phrase as it plays — 'it fades in every head at once' enacted; L10's words return at full strength against it. (4) L11-CEND finale plate: +5 % dawn lift. Keyed strictly to generations/embers/finale plates and L9 words, so the already-rendered opening/L1-L5 segments (firewide/hunter/listen plates, mood 1.0) are byte-consistent with the rest.",
   "alternatives": "New generated plates per beat (rejected — v4 builds from v3's scene per brief; plate generation is the Ep.3-style rebuild lane). Leaving L8-L10 on one static embers plate for ~13 s (the pre-doctrine state — three beats, no visual event, the piece's weakest sound-off stretch).",
   "context": "Hadi's visual-storytelling + exemplar doctrine landed mid-build (2026-10-24 ~17:35 ET): visuals are 'lazy and minimal'; every beat must carry a visual event; applied to what was still open in this build (segments line-06..endcard unrendered at that moment) without restarting finished work.",
   "why": "Sound-off, the forgetting arc is the story's villain beat; before this record it looked identical to the beats around it. The mood arc makes the villain visible and the backup's arrival a rekindling.",
   "change": "Judged by Hadi on the artifact with the rest of v4 (Action #19 sitting); values are three numbers in one engine function (plateMood) if he wants them stronger or weaker."
  },
  {
   "id": "DR-GAP-CHOREO",
   "element": "Word choreography L6-L11 + pride fixes — DECIDED per word (word-choreography + pride doctrine, 2026-10-24 ~17:43 ET)",
   "choice": "Per-word decisions (all in the engine's choreo block, applied to the still-open lines L6-L12; L1-L5 were already rendered and keep the GAP-MOTION/POPS grammar — recorded inconsistency, accepted over restarting finished work): L6 'dies;' shrinks to 0.80x, sinks 8 px, dims to 70 % — 'lives.' grows 1.18x and lifts — death and survival are performed by the words. L7 'few.' at 0.78x vs 'everyone.' at 1.22x — the audience size change happens IN word size across the L7 cut. L8 'forgetting.' flickers (opacity 0.75+0.25*sin(30t)) — the enemy intrudes unstably. L9 every word fades to 45 % AND shrinks 18 % inside its phrase (fading = disappearing, DR-GAP-VISUAL extended); L10 'hard to kill.' words deliberately hold full size/opacity against it (decided restraint = resistance), 'One' 0.90x vs 'many,' 1.25x — one becomes many in size. L11 'body.' 0.92x vs 'story' 1.15x — the second archive outweighs the first. L12: NO embellishment, decided restraint — it is the flagged banned-formula line (DR-GAP / GAP-10); its words enter uniformly and are not dressed. PRIDE FIXES applied under the same record: (1) L12's two remaining pops (the subscribe / follow words) DEMOTED to ordinary words (key false, 118->100, rust->dark ink) — under DR-GAP-POPS' own rule pops are for concept words, and the banned CTA must not carry the piece's biggest emphasis; total pops 20 -> 18. (2) Channel bug switches to dark ink (#2b2018) on the pale water and finale plates where the cream bug was near-invisible in v3 frames (t=24.0, 42.0); those plates appear only in open segments, so no rendered segment changes.",
   "alternatives": "Uniform entrance everywhere (the pre-doctrine state — undecided word behaviour = randomness under the choreography doctrine). Re-rendering L1-L5 with matching choreography (rejected — finished work is not restarted; the grammar is shared, only the per-word events are line-scoped). Choreographing L12's CTA words for flair (rejected — polishing a banned formula).",
   "context": "Hadi's word-choreography + pride doctrine landed mid-build (2026-10-24 ~17:43 ET): words must TELL the story; which words shrink/grow/flip is actively decided per beat and recorded; any visible flaw gets fixed now, not passed up.",
   "why": "Sound-off, a muted viewer now sees quantity, death, fading and survival happen to the words themselves in L6-L11 — the beats where v3's words merely appeared.",
   "change": "Judged by Hadi on the artifact (Action #19 sitting); every value is one line in the engine's choreo block or one PLAN flag if he wants any word's behaviour changed."
  },
  {
   "id": "DR-GAP-WORDS",
   "element": "Word-decision container — all 139 display words (doctrine pass, 2026-10-24 ~17:47 ET)",
   "choice": "Every word in the piece carries a recorded decision in the word_decisions array of this decisions block: 9 choreographed treatments (DR-GAP-CHOREO), 10 key pops (DR-GAP-POPS, 2 of them in L9, where they then join the fade), L9's line-wide fade+shrink (15 words in total), L10's decided hold (3 words), L12's decided restraint (13 words), and deliberate as-is for the remaining 91 — each with its story function, measured tempo (from the locked word timings) and the reason no individual event was assigned (the beat's decided event is named in every as-is entry). Coverage 139/139, counted, not asserted.",
   "alternatives": "Leaving ordinary words at engine default with no record (the pre-doctrine state — undecided word behaviour, which the word-decision-container doctrine names randomness even when it looks fine).",
   "context": "Hadi's word-decision-container refinement (2026-10-24 ~17:47 ET) of the choreography doctrine: decisions live in the video's production context (this scene file); a deliberate 'use it as is' is itself an active decision and must be recorded with its reasons.",
   "why": "Future builds of this template inherit per-word intent instead of re-deriving or accidentally losing it; the count makes the coverage auditable in QC.",
   "change": "Any word's treatment can be flipped by editing its entry + the engine's choreo block; the QC script counts the container."
  }
